The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function logger(): ErrorLoggerInterface
    {
        /** @var class-string<\Cake\Error\ErrorLoggerInterface> $class */
        $class = $this->getConfig('logger', $this->_defaultConfig['logger']);
        if (!in_array(ErrorLoggerInterface::class, class_implements($class))) {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException(
                "Cannot use {$class} as an error logger. It must implement \Cake\Error\ErrorLoggerInterface."
            );
        }

        return new $class($this->_config);
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Cake\Test\TestCase\Error\ErrorTrapTest::testLoggerConfigCompatibility`:
            
```php
    public function testLoggerConfigCompatibility()
    {
        $this->deprecated(function () {
            $trap = new ErrorTrap(['errorLogger' => ErrorLogger::class]);
            $this->assertInstanceOf(ErrorLogger::class, $trap->logger());
        });
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Should have at least one deprecation warning
Failed asserting that false is true.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
public function logger(): ErrorLoggerInterface
{
    /** @var class-string<\Cake\Error\ErrorLoggerInterface> $class */
    $class = $this->getConfig('errorLogger', $this->_defaultConfig['logger']);
    if (!in_array(ErrorLoggerInterface::class, class_implements($class))) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException(
            "Cannot use {$class} as an error logger. It must implement \Cake\Error\ErrorLoggerInterface."
        );
    }

    return new $class($this->_config);
}
```
